30,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The ground is tricky! Big digging is risky because of clay, but small work is fine. Also, the south side is easier to build on.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Interesting. My findings suggest the park is a major thoroughfare for commuters and is currently struggling with drainage and heat.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The staff is very small now. We have to buy in special care, but we do have volunteers for habitats and sports.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Minako,,"It seems our hard surfaces fail quickly, while water-based works last. However, planting fails if the contract ignores aftercare.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The funding is heavily skewed toward nature, but the long-term cost to maintain greenery is triple that of paving.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if people just walk through the middle, maybe we shouldn't put something there that blocks them?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Kenji. We need a solution that handles the water and heat without obstructing the natural flow of pedestrians.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Minato,,"If we pick something too hard to maintain, will the few staff we have left be able to handle it?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Minako,,"That is why I am wary of the planting. If we don't secure the aftercare, it will just die like the eastern avenue.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"We must balance the available funding with the reality of the upkeep ledger. Greenery is ""free"" to build but expensive to keep.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Kenji,,Maybe something that doesn't need huge digging? The firms were worried about the clay.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A paved plaza might be too hot, given the August readings, and might not solve the drainage issues.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Minato,,The volunteers for sports and habitats are a great resource. Maybe we should use them?,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Minako,,The overflow basin from years ago is still perfect. That suggests water-management schemes are our most durable option.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If we choose a high-maintenance green plan, we risk a financial crisis in three years.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm starting to think the south side is the safest bet for construction.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic suggests we need a plan that integrates drainage and respects the commuter paths.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Minato,,I think we should pick something the volunteers can help with.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Minako,,I trust the water-works. They last. I just want to ensure the maintenance is realistic.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will be looking for the most fiscally sustainable option that still utilizes the habitat fund.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
